---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_ii2_72",
  "series": "Band II 2 (1686 - 1694)",
  "seq": 72,
  "text": "<p> [[299.7]] <b>73. LEIBNIZ AN VITALE GIORDANI</p>\n<p> [[299.8]] [Rom, Mitte November 1689.] [72.]</b></p>\n<p> [[299.18]] [<i>L^#'1</i> ] </p>\n<p> [[299.19]] 1. Secundum certum considerandi modum corpus est prius superficie, et superficies prior\n[[299.20]] linea. Sunt enim termini corporis nec per se subsistunt. Unde bene ex corporis sectione\n[[299.21]] derivantur. Nec simplicior derivandi ratio est quam secando corpus indeterminatum vel cujus\n[[299.22]] termini non considerantur et ita quidem ut terminus communis seu secans utrinque se habeat\n[[299.23]] eodem modo seu secet in partes respective congruentes et tunc fit <b>planum</b>. Et si rursus tale\n[[299.24]] eodem modo secetur prodit <b>recta</b>. Quae consideratio novitate et simplicitate sua applausum\n[[299.25]] aliquem ab ingeniis mereri posse videbatur. </p>\n<p> [[299.26]] 2. Non video quomodo aliquid de recta demonstrari possit, non utendo rectae definitione\n[[299.27]] aut proprietate ulla. Sane ex demonstrationibus a Proclo aut Clavio mutuatis cognosci non\n[[300.1]] potest, utrum pertineant ad lineam antea definitam quae scilicet brevissmia est inter extrema,\n[[300.2]] nec ullam aliam rectae notionem praesupponunt. </p>\n<p> [[300.3]] [...] </p>\n<p> [[300.4]] 4. Crediderim defectum in demonstratione Thaletis sine ullo tironum praejudicio emendari\n[[300.5]] posse. </p>\n<p> [[300.6]] 5. Annotavi ista non libidine contradicendi, sed quia scio magni referre ad perfectionem\n[[300.7]] Geometriae, ut axiomata Euclidea de natura Rectae perfecte demonstrentur. </p>\n<p> [[300.8]] [<i>L^#'2</i> ] </p>\n<p> [[300.9]] [ ... ] Caeterum non is ego sum qui mea velut ex tripode dicta statim recipi velim; et\n[[300.10]] ingenuitatem eorum inprimis amo, qui non diffitentur se utiliter admonitos. Itaque quod contra\n[[300.11]] meam rectae definitionem objicis dignum consideratu agnosco; utrum scilicet in eo peccet,\n[[300.12]] quod plani et solidi notiones supponit, an potius vel ideo laudem mereatur. Quod tibi porro\n[[300.13]] examinandum relinquo exactius, antequam dicamus tecum, currum esse positum ante boves.\n[[300.14]] Erit enim qui arbitretur corporis notionem priorem esse notione superficiei et lineae, tanquam\n[[300.15]] corporis terminorum, nec per se subsistentium; et has corporis sectione cognosci. Quod initio\n[[300.16]] assumo interminatum vel ita ut termini ejus non considerentur; ita ut ipsa sectio det terminos.\n[[300.17]] Prima autem et simplicissima corporis sectio est in partes sibi respondentes congruas, seu ita ut\n[[300.18]] secans ad utramque secti partem se habeat eodem modo; et haec fit per <b>planum</b>. Et prima\n[[300.19]] rursus plani sectio eodem modo fit <b>per rectam</b>, nec (quantum ego video) nisi per rectam.\n[[300.20]] Habemus ergo plani et rectae originem simplicissimam secundum hunc considerandi modum\n[[300.21]] qui sane novus apud ingenuos aliquem applausum sperare poterat. Nec ideo alios considerandi\n[[300.22]] modos improbo (quales et ipse habeo), dummodo par claritas obtineatur, quam in Euclidea\n[[300.23]] nondum hactenus agnoveramus. Interim quacunque demum utamur notione rectae, eam\n[[300.24]] influere ut ita dicam, oportet, in theoremata quae de recta demonstrare volumus, alioqui\n[[300.25]] ignotum est, utrum ea quae demonstramus ad eam rem pertineant, cujus data est definitio. Idque\n[[300.26]] in illis demonstrationibus Euclideorum Axiomatum quas a Proclo et Clavio mutuatus es\n[[300.27]] desiderare me jam innui, etsi hoc in responsione tua praeterieris. Quomodo enim ex iis sciemus\n[[300.28]] pertinere ad lineam brevissimam inter sua puncta extrema. Caeterum cum propositum esset in\n[[300.29]] <i>Euclide</i> tuo omnia qua licet exacte demonstrare, fortasse non diffiteberis rectius suppleri casus\n[[300.30]] qui ad perfectionem demonstrationis desiderantur quod tironibus opinor praejudicium facere\n[[300.31]] non poterat. Neque quisquam unquam tam bene subductis rationibus librum scripsit quin aliqua\n[[301.1]] hujusmodi admonitionum materia supersit, quas sine detrimento existimationis agnoscere possumus.\n[[301.2]] [ ... ] Sed nolo te his tenere diutius, voluique tantum respondere, ne me putes quadam\n[[301.3]] contradicendi libidine temerarias objectiones festinasse. Nam diu desideravi exactas videre\n[[301.4]] axiomatum istorum demonstrationes quoniam sciebam magni referre ad perfectionem Geometriae,\n[[301.5]] itaque dubitationes meas vel ideo tibi proponere volebam, ut Te quem parem superandae\n[[301.6]] difficultati putabam, ad supplenda quae desunt, excitarem. Vale et me ama. </p>\n",
  "number": "73.",
  "title": "LEIBNIZ AN VITALE GIORDANI",
  "date": "[Rom, Mitte November 1689.] [72.]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:73. LEIBNIZ AN VITALE GIORDANI [Rom, Mitte November 1689.] [72.] [L^#'1 ] 1. Secundum certum considerandi modum corpus est prius superficie, et superficies prior linea. Sunt enim termini corporis nec per se subsistunt. Unde bene ex corporis sectione derivantur. Nec simplicior derivandi ratio est qua...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>